-- A 3-level clabject chain over a purely graph-theoretic domain (no
-- taxonomy, no real-world story): an abstract notion of a graph vertex,
-- refined step by step into a properly-colored, then labeled, vertex.
--   M3 Vertex         -- degree only, plus a self-association giving
--                         every vertex its neighbors.
--   M2 ColoredVertex   -- instantiates Vertex; renames "degree" to
--                         "valence" and cancels Vertex's own degree
--                         invariant at that same edge (replaced by an
--                         inter-constraint below, same pattern as
--                         MLM-USE/VehicleTaxonomy.use's wheel rename).
--   M1 LabeledVertex   -- instantiates ColoredVertex; adds nothing but
--                         a name -- included just to show a 3-deep
--                         chain still resolves everything from M3 and
--                         M2 correctly.
--
-- The two things worth studying closely here, both only representable
-- because MLM-USE (unlike CatMLM) has a real inter-constraints section:
--
--   1. NonNegativeValence has to live in inter-constraints, not in M2's
--      own "constraints" block. A constraint written directly inside
--      "model M2 ... constraints" is checked against ColoredVertex as a
--      PLAIN class, before the clabject edge below ever applies its
--      rename -- at that point ColoredVertex has no "valence" at all,
--      only its own "color". Only inter-constraints (via "M2@..") sees
--      the class *after* clabject inheritance/renaming has been
--      resolved, so that's the only place a constraint can mention an
--      inherited-and-renamed feature.
--
--   2. ProperColoring needs "oclAsType(M2@ColoredVertex)" on the
--      neighbors it navigates to. AdjacentTo is declared once, on
--      Vertex at M3, and is inherited unchanged by every level below --
--      but inheriting a role doesn't change ITS DECLARED TYPE. Statically,
--      "self.neighbors" is still a Set(M3@Vertex), even when every actual
--      vertex in the running system is really a ColoredVertex. Reading
--      ".color" off a neighbor needs an explicit multiType-qualified
--      downcast; without it, the compiler correctly refuses "color" as
--      unknown on Vertex.

MLM GraphColoring

model M3

class Vertex
attributes
  degree: Integer
end

constraints
context Vertex inv NonNegativeDegree:
  self.degree >= 0

association AdjacentTo between
  Vertex[*] role neighbors
  Vertex[*] role neighborOf
end


model M2

class ColoredVertex
attributes
  color: Integer
end

constraints
context ColoredVertex inv ValidColor:
  self.color >= 0 and self.color <= 2


model M1

class LabeledVertex
attributes
  label: String
end


inter-constraints
context M2@ColoredVertex inv NonNegativeValence:
  self.valence >= 0

context M2@ColoredVertex inv ProperColoring:
  self.neighbors->forAll(n | n.oclAsType(M2@ColoredVertex).color <> self.color)


mediator M3 < NONE
end

mediator M2 < M3
clabject ColoredVertex : Vertex
attributes
  degree -> valence
constraints
  ~NonNegativeDegree
end
end

mediator M1 < M2
clabject LabeledVertex : ColoredVertex
end
end
